{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/supabase/auth/compare/master...a39858b6e9d194198005eceff9e707c0cd3118e1","html_url":"https://github.com/supabase/auth/compare/master...a39858b6e9d194198005eceff9e707c0cd3118e1","permalink_url":"https://github.com/supabase/auth/compare/supabase:10ef107...supabase:a39858b","diff_url":"https://github.com/supabase/auth/compare/master...a39858b6e9d194198005eceff9e707c0cd3118e1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/supabase/auth/compare/master...a39858b6e9d194198005eceff9e707c0cd3118e1.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"10ef10789d1ee4fb422b448047e67e3e264c0482","node_id":"C_kwDOEKipmdoAKDEwZWYxMDc4OWQxZWU0ZmI0MjJiNDQ4MDQ3ZTY3ZTNlMjY0YzA0ODI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Cemal Kılıç","email":"cemalkilic@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-11-17T16:19:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-11-17T16:19:39Z"},"message":"feat: use client assertions in the custom OIDC token exchange (#2936)\n\n## What\n\nLast PR in the stack. For `private_key_jwt` providers, the authorization\ncode exchange sends `client_assertion` and `client_assertion_type` in\nthe form body instead of a client secret, with no Basic auth header.\n\n- Fails closed: a `private_key_jwt` provider can't be loaded when\nassertions are disabled, no signing key is configured, or the provider\nisn't OIDC, so no request goes out.\n- On `invalid_client`, the cached assertion is dropped and the rejection\nis logged without the assertion.\n- New metrics for signing latency and errors, and `invalid_client`\nresponses per provider.\n\nThe assertion has `iss` and `sub` set to the client_id (`iss` can be\noverridden), and `aud` is the issuer unless the provider sets an\naudience. Assertions are reused for up to 10 minutes and have no `jti`,\nso providers that require single-use assertions won't accept them.\n\n## Tests\n\nExact shape of the token request, cache reuse, failing closed,\n`invalid_client` handling, and an end-to-end test that loads a\n`private_key_jwt` provider and checks the exchange sends a valid\nassertion.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #2932\n1. #2933\n1. #2934\n1. #2935\n1. #2936 👈","tree":{"sha":"2c8102e2e5641316828fcef6597560121f78d6d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/supabase/auth/git/trees/2c8102e2e5641316828fcef6597560121f78d6d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/supabase/auth/git/commits/10ef10789d1ee4fb422b448047e67e3e264c0482","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq/H6bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArsoQAKKjOTvzYIL9BMyX0HFHheEH\nMxExKq1hSj97ROTSdUuk0//DXUX16NyvZoljl6B164O2KK4MC4eiI1bfPwg2TLzR\n5Unt2VCE7l0oWZmZ4XQzfqOaAhVFQXX2XglUw0mSrcYB2kEJ8oXA6M550ae6XmQy\nw3DzLKrVh6q0/zlb1j6yUApaspiqaTvmok49ilvHI+BUHlaxywcJf6Iw2D6dyrc2\nUSDqCt1Fot7BXNthDsaTDZgcBArzh14IjdFPQs32KSB55qSdWAJHhiHfTREj+rXY\nwYkp8TS8gmbiDzHxq5TIEi6ueq42fFmEw/Q4s0auMM9n98Oz7rnzwSiX6SFXQN7A\nY3KQR9axJhQmxCql1DFHJxEgbUTiWLycAQ5Rt5sPnYQOFc99lijJtG2pcQNN6xlz\nPmUKUdGNUlwlJh9go3XVWz7yxT3S+DtFy5Rl1GFP/SuwK8C2SXK5CFlLJEDB4HYI\nCQhqPZroy2imn2odALM+c48HRbNVIkziG5XyBEiqvO8T6FxMBbVZxkdSPxseRy3D\nrctw29aKEETBBigCeFWzdjjuXDH6BWZlTsXWI1dLmaDljKVT7+uCoBdFbxFRiPMo\nNMVy+Tn7hU49wcCqD1eXyxKay2ZsPcZkDCq/Zu22VlmQ0GzDSqc+v1Fe6CDBgHgY\nNfWqdHV6Z0yf2ZIPZ4ec\n=Qfuy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2c8102e2e5641316828fcef6597560121f78d6d5\nparent f78a61d55bc0cef065dea40751007a1f32de7c16\nauthor Cemal Kılıç <cemalkilic@users.noreply.github.com> 1794932379 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1794932379 +0100\n\nfeat: use client assertions in the custom OIDC token exchange (#2936)\n\n## What\n\nLast PR in the stack. For `private_key_jwt` providers, the authorization\ncode exchange sends `client_assertion` and `client_assertion_type` in\nthe form body instead of a client secret, with no Basic auth header.\n\n- Fails closed: a `private_key_jwt` provider can't be loaded when\nassertions are disabled, no signing key is configured, or the provider\nisn't OIDC, so no request goes out.\n- On `invalid_client`, the cached assertion is dropped and the rejection\nis logged without the assertion.\n- New metrics for signing latency and errors, and `invalid_client`\nresponses per provider.\n\nThe assertion has `iss` and `sub` set to the client_id (`iss` can be\noverridden), and `aud` is the issuer unless the provider sets an\naudience. Assertions are reused for up to 10 minutes and have no `jti`,\nso providers that require single-use assertions won't accept them.\n\n## Tests\n\nExact shape of the token request, cache reuse, failing closed,\n`invalid_client` handling, and an end-to-end test that loads a\n`private_key_jwt` provider and checks the exchange sends a valid\nassertion.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #2932\n1. #2933\n1. #2934\n1. #2935\n1. #2936 👈","verified_at":"2026-11-17T16:19:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/supabase/auth/commits/10ef10789d1ee4fb422b448047e67e3e264c0482","html_url":"https://github.com/supabase/auth/commit/10ef10789d1ee4fb422b448047e67e3e264c0482","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/supabase/auth/commits/10ef10789d1ee4fb422b448047e67e3e264c0482/comments","author":{"login":"cemalkilic","id":13753694,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzUzNjk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13753694?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cemalkilic","html_url":"https://github.com/cemalkilic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cemalkilic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cemalkilic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cemalkilic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cemalkilic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cemalkilic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cemalkilic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cemalkilic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cemalkilic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.githu